<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Gojo · Motifs and their connections</title><style>
:root{--ink:#25434b;--muted:#657178;--paper:#f4f0e4;--line:#c7cbd0;--accent:#9c5739}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font:17px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1400px;margin:auto;padding:35px 28px 70px}h1,h2,h3{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-weight:500;line-height:1.2}h1{font-size:44px;margin:12px 0}h2{font-size:30px}h3{font-size:23px;margin:10px 0}p{max-width:1000px}a{color:#27626e}button,select{font:inherit}button{padding:9px 14px;border:1px solid #8c9c93;border-radius:5px;background:#fffaf0;color:var(--ink);cursor:pointer}button[aria-pressed=true]{background:#25434b;color:white}button:hover{border-color:var(--accent)}.eyebrow{letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);font-size:13px}.intro{font-size:20px}.rules{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:14px;margin:24px 0}.rule{border-top:3px solid #9c5739;padding:12px 15px;background:#fffaf0}.rule strong{display:block}.rule p{font-size:15px;margin:7px 0}.example{margin:40px 0;padding:24px;background:#fffdf5;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;scroll-margin-top:15px}.example h2{margin:4px 0 12px}.purpose{color:var(--muted)}.steps{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin:20px 0}.steps button{font-size:15px}.question{border-left:4px solid #536d87;background:#eef1f4;padding:16px 20px;font-size:20px;min-height:110px}.question p{margin:3px 0}.question small{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px;margin:20px 0}.candidate{padding:17px;border:2px solid var(--line);background:#fffdf8;border-radius:5px;min-width:0}.candidate.only-retained{border-color:#496d95;border-top-width:5px}.candidate.retained{border-color:#758aa1}.candidate.excluded{border-style:dashed;border-color:#93989e}.candidate.unresolved{border-style:dotted;border-color:#93989e}.candidate .badge{display:inline-block;padding:5px 9px;margin-bottom:10px;border-radius:3px;background:#eef0f2;color:#414f5b;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.045em;font-weight:700}.candidate.only-retained .badge,.candidate.retained .badge{background:#e5edf6;color:#294f76}.candidate.excluded .badge{background:repeating-linear-gradient(135deg,#edf0f2,#edf0f2 5px,#e3e7ea 5px,#e3e7ea 7px)}.candidate img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;margin:14px 0}.candidate-answer{font-weight:650;margin:8px 0}.candidate-status{font-size:15px;margin:8px 0}.reason{font-size:14px;color:#46525c;margin:10px 0}.answer-history{table-layout:fixed;font-size:13px;margin:16px 0 5px}.answer-history caption{text-align:left;font-weight:650;padding-bottom:5px}.answer-history th,.answer-history td{padding:6px 4px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.answer-history thead th{background:#f0f2f4;font-size:12px;font-weight:600}.answer-history tbody th{background:transparent}.answer-history th:first-child{width:12%}.answer-history th:nth-child(2),.answer-history th:nth-child(3){width:24%}.answer-history th:nth-child(4){width:40%}.answer-history .current{background:#f0f4f8}.history-difference{font-weight:700}.answer-scope{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin:4px 0}.vocabulary{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);padding-top:12px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:15px}.source{padding:12px 18px;background:#f0eee4;border:1px dashed var(--line)}.source img{display:block;max-width:560px;width:100%;margin:12px auto}.finding{border-left:4px solid var(--accent);padding:7px 16px;color:#654a3b}.controls{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:16px}.control{border:1px dashed #ad8d52;background:#f8f0de;padding:20px}.table-wrap{overflow:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:15px}th,td{text-align:left;padding:9px 11px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}th{background:#e8e8da}.status{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}details{margin:15px 0}summary{cursor:pointer}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}.limits li{margin:8px 0}footer{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:35px;padding-top:18px;color:var(--muted);font-size:15px}
@media(max-width:1000px){.rules{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.cards{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:640px){main{padding:22px 14px 45px}h1{font-size:34px}.example{padding:15px}.rules,.cards,.controls{grid-template-columns:1fr}.question{padding:13px;font-size:18px}.steps button{max-width:100%;text-align:left}h2{font-size:26px}}
</style></head><body><main>
<div class="eyebrow">Gojo · pre-numeric structural experiments</div><h1 id="heading">A motif is only the beginning</h1>
<p class="intro" id="intro">Can the same small motif vocabulary describe <em>copies and their relationships</em>? These cases separate a loop's existence from its multiplicity, shared corners, shared edges and path contacts.</p>
<p id="mechanism">The engine reads native segments, shared-site identities and coarse directions. Questions request the illustrated motifs with their heading patterns, rather than every possible polygon or rotation. These are local analysis tests over exposed inventories; the pictures are illustrations made afterwards. Matching receives no pixels, screen coordinates or construction history.</p>
<div class="rules" id="rules"><div class="rule"><strong>1 · Bind a role</strong><p>Find an actual occurrence of a supplied native motif.</p></div><div class="rule"><strong>2 · Keep copies distinct</strong><p>Different starts or reverse readings of one loop still use the same actual edges.</p></div><div class="rule"><strong>3 · Ask about sharing</strong><p>Require a shared site or edge, or require that selected roles stay disjoint.</p></div><div class="rule"><strong>4 · Preserve an open read</strong><p>Without enough search or the right evidence, do not turn “not found” into “No”.</p></div></div>
<p><strong>Two separate reads:</strong> <em>Answer to this question</em> is the candidate's Yes, No or Open. The badge above each drawing says whether that candidate is <em>retained after all replies so far</em>. Blue emphasizes retained candidates; a dashed outline marks an exclusion. Answer values have no status colour. Each card shows the observed and candidate answers side by side, including any earlier difference. Solid copper dots mark actual joins; paired hollow purple dots mark separate identities at the same displayed position.</p>
<div id="cases"></div>
<h2>Incomplete-read controls</h2><p>These control reads should stay Open. Completing one stage does not supply unfinished assignments, correspondences or an unpublished selection.</p><div id="controls" class="controls"></div>
<section id="scaling-section"><h2>Small scaling check</h2><p>These inputs contain separate identical triangle loops. Finding a pair can finish early. Proving that no pair shares a site needs more assignments. A small joint budget stops that search with an Open answer.</p>
<p class="status">Each row is one local diagnostic run, after a warm-up. “Attempts” counts attempted role extensions, including rejected partial assignments. The budget does not bound motif induction or preparation. Timings exclude drawing and archive work; they are not a throughput benchmark.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table id="scaling"><thead><tr><th>Loops</th><th>Question</th><th>Budget</th><th>Answer</th><th>Attempts</th><th>Inventory ms</th><th>Joint read ms</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div></section>
<h2>What this establishes—and what stays open</h2><ul id="limits" class="limits"></ul>
<details><summary>Native archive and reproduction</summary><p id="native"></p><p><a id="archive-link" href="composition.gojo.json.gz">Full native study archive</a> · <a href="diagnostics.json">Derived report data</a> · <a id="documentation-link" href="../../../../Gojo/docs/GojoOccurrenceCompositionExperiments.md">Experiment explanation</a></p><p><code id="command">dotnet run --project experiments/QualitativeFrieze -c Release -- --occurrence-composition</code></p></details>
<footer><a id="previous-link" href="../structural-evidence/gallery.html">Earlier single-motif question experiments</a> · No new kernel primitive, model fitting or cloud computation in this run.</footer>
</main><script type="application/json" id="data">__DATA__</script><script>
'use strict'; const model=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('data').textContent);
const esc=s=>String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));
const presentation=model.presentation||{};
for(const [key,id] of [['heading','heading'],['intro','intro'],['mechanism','mechanism'],['command','command']])if(presentation[key])document.getElementById(id).textContent=presentation[key];
if(presentation.title)document.title=presentation.title;
if(presentation.rules)document.getElementById('rules').innerHTML=presentation.rules.map(r=>`<div class="rule"><strong>${esc(r.title)}</strong><p>${esc(r.text)}</p></div>`).join('');
for(const [key,id] of [['archiveName','archive-link'],['documentation','documentation-link'],['previousLink','previous-link']])if(presentation[key])document.getElementById(id).setAttribute('href',presentation[key]);
if(presentation.previousLabel)document.getElementById('previous-link').textContent=presentation.previousLabel;
if(!(model.scaling||[]).length)document.getElementById('scaling-section').hidden=true;
const findings={C01:'Existence alone loses multiplicity. Two distinct roles establish at least two loops; a third role can test the next lower bound. None of these claims gives an exact global count.',C02:'Two closed contours can remain distinct while sharing a corner. Sharing a site and reusing an edge are separate questions.',C03:'A shared edge is one actual participant reused by both loops. Two overlapping but separately drawn edges do not satisfy that question.',C04:'These examples differ at the path’s endpoint joins. The current query checks shared sites anywhere in each motif; it does not specifically require endpoints. A middle vertex could satisfy contact too.',C05:'The near and far arrangements remain possible. Spacing was removed from the exposed observation, so this reader has no evidence to prefer either.'};
function render(example,index){const stage=example.stages[index],article=document.querySelector(`[data-case="${example.id}"]`);article.dataset.stage=index;
 article.querySelectorAll('[data-step]').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(Number(b.dataset.step)===index)));
 const work=stage.correspondenceAttempts>0?`${stage.attempts} role assignments and ${stage.correspondenceAttempts} landmark correspondence steps in the source read.`:`${stage.attempts} attempted role extensions in the source read.`;
 const q=article.querySelector('.question');q.innerHTML=index===0?'<p><strong>Start: no compound questions yet</strong></p><p>No observed facts have been requested. All supplied alternatives are untested.</p>':`<p><strong>Current question: ${esc(stage.question)}</strong></p><p>Observed answer: <strong>${esc(stage.sourceAnswer)}</strong></p><p class="answer-scope">After all ${index} repl${index===1?'y':'ies'}: ${stage.compatible.length} candidate${stage.compatible.length===1?' is':'s are'} retained.</p><small>${work} Earlier replies remain part of the comparison.</small>`;
 article.querySelector('.cards').innerHTML=example.candidates.map(candidate=>{
  const read=stage.reads.find(r=>r.index===candidate.index),resolved=index>0&&stage.compatible.length===1&&read.isSettled&&read.isCompatible;
  const earlier=example.stages.slice(1,index+1);
  const mismatch=earlier.find(s=>{const a=s.reads.find(r=>r.index===candidate.index).answer;return ['Yes','No'].includes(a)&&['Yes','No'].includes(s.sourceAnswer)&&a!==s.sourceAnswer});
  const cls=index===0?'untested':!read.isCompatible?'excluded':!read.isSettled?'unresolved':resolved?'only-retained':'retained';
  const badge=index===0?'UNTESTED':!read.isCompatible?`EXCLUDED${mismatch?` AT STEP ${mismatch.index}`:''}`:!read.isSettled?'UNRESOLVED':resolved?'ONLY RETAINED CANDIDATE':'RETAINED';
  const status=index===0?'No replies compared yet.':!read.isCompatible?'An earlier or current reply excludes this candidate.':!read.isSettled?'Retained provisionally; some evidence remains open.':resolved?'Agrees with all replies received; no alternative remains.':'Agrees with all replies received.';
  const currentAgrees=index>0&&['Yes','No'].includes(read.answer)&&read.answer===stage.sourceAnswer;
  const reason=mismatch?`<p class="reason">Step ${mismatch.index} excludes it: observed <strong>${esc(mismatch.sourceAnswer)}</strong>, candidate <strong>${esc(mismatch.reads.find(r=>r.index===candidate.index).answer)}</strong>.${mismatch.index<index&&currentAgrees?' Its answer agrees at this step; the earlier difference still excludes it.':''}</p>`:'';
  const history=earlier.length?`<table class="answer-history"><caption>Replies compared so far</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Step</th><th scope="col">Observed</th><th scope="col">Candidate</th><th scope="col">Comparison</th></tr></thead><tbody>${earlier.map(s=>{const a=s.reads.find(r=>r.index===candidate.index).answer;const known=['Yes','No'].includes(a)&&['Yes','No'].includes(s.sourceAnswer),same=known&&a===s.sourceAnswer;return `<tr class="${s.index===index?'current ':''}${known&&!same?'history-difference':''}" data-history-step="${s.index}"><th scope="row" title="${esc(s.question)}">${s.index}</th><td>${esc(s.sourceAnswer)}</td><td>${esc(a)}</td><td>${known?(same?'Agrees':'Differs'):'Open'}</td></tr>`}).join('')}</tbody></table>`:'';
  const label=candidate.name;
  return `<div class="candidate ${cls}" data-candidate="${candidate.index}" data-status="${cls}"><div class="badge">${esc(badge)}</div><h3>${candidate.index+1}. ${esc(label)}</h3><img src="${esc(candidate.image)}" alt="${esc(label)}"><p class="candidate-answer">Answer to this question: <strong>${index===0?'Not yet asked':esc(read.answer)}</strong></p><p class="candidate-status">${esc(status)}</p>${reason}${history}<div class="vocabulary">Earlier existential motif vocabulary: <strong>${esc(candidate.earlierVocabulary)}</strong>.<br>This compares presence of local motif types, not how many copies exist.</div></div>`}).join('');
 article.querySelector('.finding').textContent=index===example.stages.length-1?(example.finding||findings[example.id]||example.questionPurpose):'Step through the questions to inspect which distinctions become justified.';}
document.getElementById('cases').innerHTML=model.cases.map(example=>`<article class="example" data-case="${esc(example.id)}"><div class="eyebrow">${esc(example.id)} · ${example.expectedAmbiguity?'expected ambiguity':'structural distinction'}</div><h2>${esc(example.name)}</h2><p>${esc(example.description)}</p><p class="purpose">${esc(example.questionPurpose)}</p><div class="steps">${example.stages.map((s,i)=>`<button data-step="${i}" aria-pressed="false">${i===0?'0 · Start':`${i} · ${esc(s.question)}`}</button>`).join('')}</div><div class="question" aria-live="polite"></div><div class="cards"></div><p class="finding"></p><details class="source"><summary>Inspect the source after the read</summary><p>${esc(example.source.name)}. This independently executed sample supplied the source answers.</p><img src="${esc(example.source.image)}" alt="${esc(example.source.name)}"></details></article>`).join('');
for(const example of model.cases){const article=document.querySelector(`[data-case="${example.id}"]`);article.querySelectorAll('[data-step]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>render(example,Number(b.dataset.step)));render(example,example.stages.length-1);}
document.getElementById('controls').innerHTML=model.controls.map(c=>`<article class="control"><h3>${esc(c.name)}</h3><p>Answer: <strong>${esc(c.answer)}</strong> · ${c.attempts} role extensions${c.correspondenceAttempts>0?` · ${c.correspondenceAttempts} correspondence steps`:''}</p><p>${esc(c.purpose)}</p></article>`).join('');
document.querySelector('#scaling tbody').innerHTML=model.scaling.map(r=>`<tr><td>${r.copies}</td><td>${esc(r.question)}</td><td>${r.assignmentCapacity}</td><td>${esc(r.answer)}</td><td>${r.attempts}</td><td>${r.inductionMilliseconds.toFixed(3)}</td><td>${r.jointMilliseconds.toFixed(3)}</td></tr>`).join('');
document.getElementById('limits').innerHTML=model.limits.map(s=>`<li>${esc(s)}</li>`).join('');document.getElementById('native').textContent=`${model.nativeElements.toLocaleString()} native participants, ${model.nativeNumericElements} measured numeric participants; complete archive restored. Study build ${model.buildMilliseconds.toFixed(1)} ms, including execution, inventory reads, comparisons and scaling diagnostics; excludes presentation and archive.`;
const requested=new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('case');if(requested){const target=[...document.querySelectorAll('[data-case]')].find(e=>e.dataset.case===requested);if(target)target.scrollIntoView();}
</script></body></html>
""".Replace("__DATA__", json);
}
